``` DEPLOYABLE TEMPLATE. Splunk, CIM-aligned field names. Not run in CI.
    Adapt the index/sourcetype and the lookups to your file-access data.

    Crown-jewel bulk pull: a burst of high-sensitivity downloads or copies.
    ATT&CK T1213 Data from Information Repositories, T1567 Exfiltration Over Web Service.
    D3FEND User Behavior Analysis.

    Enrichment, which raw logs do not carry:
      sensitivity  from a lookup 'sensitive_resources.csv' (object -> sensitivity).
    CIM fields used: user, object, action, bytes_out. ```
index=your_fileaccess_index action IN (download, copy, sync)
| lookup sensitive_resources.csv object OUTPUT sensitivity
| where sensitivity>=3
| eval mb_out=bytes_out/1048576
| where mb_out>=100
| stats sum(mb_out) as mb_total count as events by user, object
| where mb_total>=100
| sort - mb_total
